  "findings": [
    "Current standard 0.6.26 remains unqualified: Mac/Linux unsplit and both split placements agree exactly on all 55 prefixes but fail 56 of 110 frozen comparisons.",
    "Retained 0.6.12 passes three first-prefix comparisons but fails 15 of 55 complete Mac fixed-prefix comparisons, peak 0.003875255584716797.",
    "First old/current difference occurs at layer.0.attn.qkv_proj after identical embedding and input normalization outputs.",
    "Independent Float64 projection shows current ordered-FMA Q4 accumulation improves accuracy relative to retained 0.6.12; reverting it would sacrifice independent accuracy.",
    "Experimental compensated Q4 accumulation improves the captured full projection. A branch protecting the final reduction residual produces nearest-F32 Float64-reference outputs identically on both GPUs for this capture.",
    "Experimental modified-archive Mac full replay still fails 26 of 55 comparisons, peak 0.002151966094970703. This is not a qualified correction.",
    "Observing compensated internal sums perturbs Mac outputs by at most 1.9073486328125e-6; those traces diagnose a reduction boundary, not unchanged model behavior.",
    "The earlier 0.6.12 trace completed GPU execution but failed receipt postprocessing with a stack overflow from Math.max spread; the later runner uses bounded scalar reduction and retains each result before validation.",
    "The baseline isolated Q4 shader exactly reproduces current full-model capture but intentionally fails the correction-only tighter accuracy assertion.",
    "Earlier split.10 archive reproduces the frozen reference exactly after the initial request: all 53 subsequent first-pass prefixes plus both repeated first-request prefixes match bit-for-bit. The initial two cold prefixes fail substantially.",
    "Both experimental full native model controls fail 26/55 unchanged-reference comparisons, peak 0.002151966094970703; their complete logits are being checked for cross-platform equality.",
    "Both experimental complete controls agree bit-for-bit on all 55 frozen prefixes and the repeated two-step request, despite the unchanged-reference failure.",
    "Warm split.10 public generation observation has no numerical effect, and frozen-prefill logits match exactly. Captured input normalization is the first old/current divergence, peak 4.76837158203125e-7 on identical embedding operands.",
    "Native pipeline observation identifies 245 main_subgroup selections in split.10 and 245 declared main selections in current 0.6.26. The independent normalization oracle improves peak error from 5.143836663279444e-7 to 4.354780891446808e-7.",
    "Changing only the retained split.10 subgroup registry entry from main_subgroup to the manifest-declared main, with unchanged shader source, causes 16/55 warm fixed-prefix comparisons to exceed 0.001; peak 0.0017681121826171875. All 2793 observed normalization selections use main. This is a test-only historical control, not a production policy change."
